{
  "id": "rubocop_rubocop_15436",
  "repo_name": "rubocop/rubocop",
  "repo_url": "https://github.com/rubocop/rubocop",
  "base_commit": "72d7666db333c45b63a235e745148f8e3dfda775",
  "pr_number": 15436,
  "issue_number": 14983,
  "issue_title": "A proposal to implement cop lazy loading",
  "issue_body": "I've been inspired by slow RuboCop startup time to reduce the number of `require`s when `lib/rubocop.rb` is loaded. Right now, [more than 800 `require`s happen](https://github.com/rubocop/rubocop/blob/5e8e49241a0e95121dd9977cd8e305e3a871639f/lib/rubocop.rb), most of which are cops (700+, including correctors and mixins).\n\nWhen running RuboCop against a single file, most of the time is spent requiring the cops (even if I run only one cop or one department):\n<img width=\"1440\" height=\"726\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/777047ec-362a-4540-82bb-874e664f1680\" />\n\nWhen you have plugins (e.g. `rubocop-rails`, `rubocop-rspec`, etc.), the amount of time spent requiring cops is even greater (my project has around 1k cops available).\n\nI came up with [an (unpolished) proof of concept](https://github.com/lovro-bikic/rubocop/compare/90c795960da9c7fbd40b16f3b245eb26a6d564fa...3909cc5efad1adfc25605dfca63434468b6b6fa0) to autoload cops. This is the profile when running RuboCop against a single file and single cop with the PoC (same command as for the profile above):\n<img width=\"1440\" height=\"727\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f78f0bdd-568a-4794-9de1-2c09e6932e3e\" />\n\nTo benchmark it, I timed `rubocop -x file.rb` (run and autocorrect only the Layout department on a single file) 30 times on master and on the PoC. Here are the results:\n```\n# Master\nAverage time (s): 1.46485\nStd deviation (s): 0.0279817\n\n# PoC\nAverage time (s): 1.02049\nStd deviation (s): 0.00637835\n```\n\nThe speed-up is around 30% in this scenario. Note that in this benchmark I loaded just RuboCop; with plugins the difference would be even bigger.\n\nFor RuboCop commands which don't run only some cops or departments (e.g. just `bundle exec rubocop`), the speed-up depends on the number of enabled cops in the config. For example, I have one project which enables 45% of cops, and another which enables around 80%. [Standard base config](https://github.com/standardrb/standard/blob/0fa2bfd8ac000169b72f9608118501acac066c93/config/base.yml) enables 59% cops at the time of writing.\n\nBefore I open any PRs, I'd like to run the plan by the maintainers. Here's the general idea:\n1. Modify [RuboCop::Cop::Registry](https://github.com/rubocop/rubocop/blob/master/lib/rubocop/cop/registry.rb) so that cops can be registered only by [badge](https://github.com/rubocop/rubocop/blob/master/lib/rubocop/cop/badge.rb) and class name, which is resolved only when the cop class is needed. See changes [here](https://github.com/lovro-bikic/rubocop/compare/90c795960da9c7fbd40b16f3b245eb26a6d564fa...3909cc5efad1adfc25605dfca63434468b6b6fa0#diff-dc00dfc3fe3e605382e6da43bf62ffda83cf5f54df0bbf4d2ab986b7f072a070)\n2. Modify [RuboCop::Runner](https://github.com/rubocop/rubocop/blob/5e8e49241a0e95121dd9977cd8e305e3a871639f/lib/rubocop/runner.rb) to mobilize cops by badge instead of by class (see [here](https://github.com/lovro-bikic/rubocop/compare/90c795960da9c7fbd40b16f3b245eb26a6d564fa...3909cc5efad1adfc25605dfca63434468b6b6fa0#diff-f07569e73a97eee6d81f8777de0661110e1a3453e4ee00ae78206eeda657e883))\n3. Change cop requires into autoloads with an `autoload_cop` helper (it [`autoload`s](https://docs.ruby-lang.org/en/4.0/Kernel.html#method-i-autoload) the class and registers the cop in the registry as an autoloaded cop). See example [here](https://github.com/lovro-bikic/rubocop/compare/90c795960da9c7fbd40b16f3b245eb26a6d564fa...3909cc5efad1adfc25605dfca63434468b6b6fa0#diff-65bea20efcb72dcc36c89bcb9404d04ce3e0b9a8ecdc70317dfb4b2b180aa472)\n\nGood news is that this can be done in a backward compatible way (registry can support both required and autoloaded cops at the same time; cops can be migrated to autoloading department by department). Other good news is that it can be done in multiple small PRs.\n\nWhere this optimization will show:\n- when running against a single cop or a subset of cops (e.g. `-x` flag)\n- when the config enables only a percentage of cops (the lower the better)\n\nI should point out that the optimization will **not** eradicate cop requiring when cache can be used and cops don't have to run. This is because [`external_dependency_checksum` has to be calculated](https://github.com/rubocop/rubocop/blob/5e8e49241a0e95121dd9977cd8e305e3a871639f/lib/rubocop/cop/team.rb#L128-L135) for cops used in the run, and the only way to do that is to require the cops. However, no cops from RuboCop itself implement `#external_dependency_checksum`, and in the RuboCop org only [`rubocop-rails` implements it](https://github.com/search?q=org%3Arubocop%20external_dependency_checksum&type=code) ([for 9 cops at the moment](https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Arubocop%2Frubocop-rails%20%22include%20ActiveRecordHelper%22&type=code)), so we can think about ways to load only those cops somehow on cached runs, but I'm not sure about the approach at the moment.\n\nI should also note that plugins would have to be migrated to the `autoload_cop` helper in order to reap the full benefits of this. Since most of them are in the RuboCop org, this shouldn't be a big problem, only a lot of work, [which I don't mind](https://lovro-bikic.github.io/300-days-of-rubocop/) :D\n\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-15T05:19:22Z",
